From 7a21704a615ce265792ab02d4fbfe28135ec8a17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LS1046A Canonical <canonical@ls1046a-build>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:16:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dpaa: ethtool ntuple -> enhanced external-hash bridge (F-241)

The RM-style CC match-table walker does not exist in the 210.10.1
microcode (decomp/findings.md 2026-09-05 entries 10-16): the 0109 CC-tree
bridge parsed as a degenerate en_exthash_node and delivered every frame
to the rule queue FQID without content gating. Re-architect the bridge
onto the enhanced external-hash machine - the substrate the vendor's
cdx.ko classifies production traffic through and ask.ko's flow
acceleration already uses:

- fman_pcd_fe_flow_action gains rx_fqid: an explicit per-record RX
  reinjection FQID for the plain ENQUEUE_PKT terminal (the ethtool -N
  action queue). Zero preserves the F-188/F-193 default (tx_fqid ?:
  port default) byte-identically for ask.ko.
- fman_pcd_fe_flow_add resolves hit_fqid = rx_fqid ?: tx_fqid ?:
  target_fqid; the L2/TX terminal stays gated on tx_fqid alone.
- dpaa_cls_* rewrites: every rule becomes an exact-key en_ehash_entry
  (PORT_ID=0x00|SIP|DIP|PROTO|SPORT|DPORT, 14 bytes) with ENQUEUE_PKT
  to the rule's queue FQID; fe_engage once per port (idempotent,
  shared with ask.ko); per-key fman_pcd_fe_flow_del; exact-only
  validation (-EOPNOTSUPP fails closed for masks, per the plan's
  governing constraint). cls_tree_installed -> cls_fe_engaged.

Patch-Name: 0194-dpaa-ethtool-ntuple-ehash-bridge.patch
---
